1
00:05:28,571 --> 00:05:34,571
When the law became corrupt, outlaws became heroes.

2
00:10:57,142 --> 00:11:03,142
Lawless is a crime, drama, western film directed by John Hillcoat.

3
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:31,714
In 1931, the Bondurant brothers of Franklin County, Virginia, run a multipurpose
backwoods establishment that hides their true business — bootlegging.

4
00:21:54,285 --> 00:22:00,285
Middle brother Forrest is the brain of the operation; older
Howard is the brawn, and younger Jack, the lookout.

5
00:27:22,857 --> 00:27:28,857
Though the local police have taken bribes and left the brothers alone, a violent war erupts when a
sadistic lawman from Chicago arrives and tries to shut down the Bondurants operation.

6
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:57,428
Jack Bondurant, played by Shia LaBeouf.

7
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Forrest Bondurant, played by Tom Hardy.

8
00:43:48,571 --> 00:43:54,571
Floyd Banner, played by Gary Oldman.

9
00:49:17,142 --> 00:49:23,142
Charlie Rakes, played by Guy Pearce.

10
00:54:45,714 --> 00:54:51,714
Howard Bondurant, played by Jason Clarke.

11
01:00:14,285 --> 01:00:20,285
Maggie Beauford, played by Jessica Chastain.

12
01:05:42,857 --> 01:05:48,857
Lawless is a 2012 American gangster film directed by John Hillcoat.

13
01:11:11,428 --> 01:11:17,428
The screenplay, by Australian singer-screenwriter Nick Cave, is based on Matt
Bondurant's historical novel The Wettest County in the World (2008).

14
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The film stars Shia LaBeouf, Tom Hardy, Gary Oldman, Mia
Wasikowska, Jessica Chastain, Jason Clarke, and Guy Pearce.

15
01:22:08,571 --> 01:22:14,571
The film is about the violent conflict between three bootlegging brothers: Forrest (Hardy), Howard (Clarke), and Jack Bondurant (LaBeouf) — and the corrupt and
ruthless lawman Charlie Rakes (Pearce), who tries to shut down the brothers' Prohibition-era moonshine business after Forrest refuses to pay him off.

16
01:27:37,142 --> 01:27:43,142
The film was in development for about three years before being produced.

17
01:33:05,714 --> 01:33:11,714
It screened at the 2012 Cannes Film Festival and was theatrically
released on August 29, 2012 by The Weinstein Company.

18
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed
$54.4 million against a $26 million budget.

19
01:44:02,857 --> 01:44:08,857
The film explores themes of corruption, based on novel or
book, prohibition era, brother, gangster.

20
01:49:31,428 --> 01:49:37,428
The tone is dark and emotional.
